 native_checks='All four new native imports passed with zero fatal shape errors and zero shape warning messages. Shape checking was ON in PREP7 during import and CHECK and retained in the saved database. No warning was suppressed and no shape threshold changed. The redundant unsupported SHPP command from the older C02 SOLU template was omitted; this changes no numerical meaning because shape checking is already enabled in the valid processor. Gmsh parameter-metadata warnings are logged separately and are not native element shape warnings. Historical C02 retains its original warning record without modification.'
 BVP='All sources use E = 210,000 MPa, nu = 0.30, small-strain isotropic elasticity, STATIC, NLGEOM OFF, PCG tolerance 1e-8 and two CPUs. These are numerical assumptions rather than measured specimen material constants. Nominal 100 MPa times documented nominal 19 mm times the verified full 28 mm Y span gives 53,200 N at each end, with opposite global-X signs. This is a reference load, not the original fatigue load. No arbitrary full-face clamp, additional lateral restraint or centroid recentering was introduced.\n\nEach source has its own common constant-X load line: Ymid and Z = fitted parent at (Xmid,Ymid) minus half the true-normal thickness offset. G08 retains its different design-X origin; C02 coordinates are not copied. Affine traction b=[1,Y-Yline,Z-Zline], M=integral(b b^T)dA, M c=[signed F,0,0], is consistently integrated over actual quadratic Tri6 ports. An independent 36-point Gauss/Duffy calculation checks the seven-point Dunavant assembly. Actual port areas, traction ranges and coefficients are supplied in STANDARDIZED_LOAD_PORTS.csv; blanket 100 MPa traction was not assumed to give the required force.\n\nSix scalar gauges at three left corners remove exactly six rigid modes: rear/Ymin UX,UY,UZ; rear/Ymax UX,UZ; front/Ymin UX. Both mesh levels use identical geometric gauge locations and DOFs. Per-port applied force/moment residuals pass 1e-8, using F and F t denominators.'
