 equilibrium='Signed applied forces and reactions are added; applied and reaction moments use the same actual nodal coordinates and source-specific origin. The equilibrium denominators are F=53,200 N and F t=1,010,800 N mm. Both prescribed reaction tolerances are 1e-5. Self-equilibrated end loading should leave near-zero resultant gauge reactions. All constrained gauge displacements are zero; no uncontrolled rigid motion was detected.\n\n'+mdtable(eq,['source_id','level','force_residual','moment_residual_Ft','Umax_mm','UXmax_mm','UYmax_mm','UZmax_mm','gauge_motion_mm'])
 tensor='Targets are computed from actual solved SOLID187 displacement fields: quadratic shape derivatives, actual Jacobian, global displacement gradient, infinitesimal strain, isotropic C:strain, six physical stress components and maximum tensile principal stress. The eigenvalue is clipped to tension before averaging. No stored reference labels or nearest-node stress copying are used. Independent scalar-loop/Voigt recovery checks 256 deterministic original-source points per level with the inherited 1e-7 MPa tolerance. Native ETABLE element averages are also compared with four-Gauss-point direct stress means, recognizing their field interpretation; native extrapolated nodal averages are not substituted for direct source-point recovery.\n\n'+mdtable(number_rows('TENSOR_INDEPENDENT_CHECKS.csv'),['source_id','level','independent_direct_tensor_max_error_MPa','native_ETABLE_max_error_MPa','native_ETABLE_relative_L2'])
 mapping='Each level maps all 39,200 intended halo source queries with zero failures and 100% area-weighted coverage. The frozen halo excludes X-port distances below 10 mm and Y-edge distances below 2 mm. The frozen T2 core uses 11 mm and 3 mm. All 34,200 core source IDs remain valid on both levels. Core area is 865.356547363 mm2 for G08 and 877.963025749 mm2 for X10, about 51.10% and 51.36% of each full measured front area. This is complete coverage of the prospectively defined support, not a claim that every exterior point has a stress label. Exterior 29,257 source points remain NOT_QUERIED; they are retained with blank stresses. Full-front geometry fidelity was nevertheless audited separately.\n\nActual quadratic surface inverse-XY correspondence is used, with barycentric inclusion tolerance 1e-5 and maximum distance 0.04 mm. Original source XYZ are not moved. Host element IDs, face IDs, barycentric coordinates, actual FE projection and projection distances are retained in each source mapping package. Different mesh-node sets do not redefine the source support.'
 T2='For every core point, use the original same-front-face 3D Euclidean chord neighborhood of radius 1.0 mm (+1e-7 mm search tolerance), unchanged T0 area weights and complete valid-weight fraction at least 1-1e-10. Maximum tensile principal stress is computed before scalar averaging. No tensor-first averaging, 2D projected-distance substitution, target smoothing or stress-dependent query selection was applied. Geometry-only parent/weld/collar proxies were frozen before stresses and are not validated physical toe tracks.\n\nFine M2 is the denominator for normalized field L2, matching the inherited FE convention. High95 uses the interpolated area-weighted CDF, explicitly separate from ML stable-step quantiles. Independent scalar neighborhood checks satisfy 1e-8 MPa. Whole/regional L2, all requested additional final statistics, high95 precision/recall, quantiles and centroids were reproduced through separate scalar arithmetic.\n\n'+mdtable(metrics,['source_id','M1_mean_T2_MPa','M2_mean_T2_MPa','mean_signed_M2_minus_M1_MPa','MAE_MPa','RMSE_MPa','whole_L2','worst_regional_L2','high95_area_IoU'])
 qual='Frozen gates are whole normalized T2 L2 <=0.020, worst regional L2 <=0.030, high95 area IoU >=0.800 and mapping/common-core coverage >=0.990, together with all independent geometry, native, equilibrium, tensor and complete-neighborhood gates. Both new targets passed every mandatory scientific gate. No source was qualified merely because a solver completed or two meshes agreed.\n\n'+result_table+'\n\n'+mdtable(metrics,['source_id','high95_precision','high95_recall','M2_Q95_T2_MPa','M2_max_T2_MPa','M2_nominal_Kmax','high95_centroid_shift_mm','common_source_IDs','common_area_mm2'])
